    "findings": [
      "G1 introduces the concrete value-created/workers/capital operation before defining the residual, and explains fictional links and nominal amounts before the equations.",
      "The introduction explains the purpose of materials, investment/continuation, labor separation and linked equations before naming their methods.",
      "The roadmap connects measure definition, source restrictions, estimation, shared-record comparison and sensitivity to the opening distinction between coverage and comparability.",
      "LP and OP each present source variables, calendar timing and unavailable-input counts before their estimation equations.",
      "Whole-history resampling and the distinction between standard error and percentile intervals appear before the first coefficient table.",
      "Source-bound own/common counts remain distinct; annual predictions use fixed pooled slopes/reference, preserve calendar gaps and do not claim separate annual technologies or real productivity growth.",
      "The actual G0 prose similarly moves from an evidence-supported distinction to source/measurement limits and construction, then interpretation. G1 uses that reasoning order while retaining method-specific technical depth."
    ],
